      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:un20bp'
    'female|a||What it does not promise is any single draw: one draw can miss by four, either way. That is chance, and bigger groups shrink it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:16e4e6x'
    'female|a||What it does promise reaches everything in the columns: motivation, family, a diagnosis nobody wrote down. Matching people on what you measured cannot promise that.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19gv5i5'
    female|a||A new case. A clinic can send a nurse to half its diabetic patients. Which way of choosing them makes the two columns independent of the choice?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1id9873'
    'female|a||The computer draw: it cannot see how anyone would fare, so both columns match on average in the two groups.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||With six made-up people we could check, because we invented the columns. With ninety thousand real ones, how would anyone know the draw was fair?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Oregon ran a real draw of this kind, and everything it found rests on that draw having been fair. So how would anyone check?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||It began in early 2008, when the state had money to add about ten thousand low-income adults to Medicaid, and in five weeks about ninety thousand put their names down.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1eumaom'
    female|a||Between March and September it drew names in eight rounds, about thirty-five thousand in all, and only those drawn could apply.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jmnxtz'
    female|a||The two columns are as hidden here as anywhere, so the check uses what was fixed before the draw, which winning could not change.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jym61a'
    female|a||First, nine answers from the sign-up form, like age, sex, language, and whether they signed up on the very first day. Then twelve measures of hospital use from state records, for the months before.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1tptwey'
    'female|a||And one test of all of them together: do they, jointly, predict who was drawn?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12wu9oq'
    female|a||In Oregon they do not. The p-value is point two four for the form, point eight four for the hospital records, and point five six for all of them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6jot25'
    female|a||Differences that size turn up by chance alone a quarter of the time or more, even with a perfectly fair draw.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15msq65'
    'female|a||A crooked draw would look different: winners younger, fewer past hospital stays, quicker to sign up, every gap leaning the same way.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1k67soj'
    'female|a||Each joint test would then fall below one in a thousand: whatever sorted the two groups, it was not chance.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1684v4j'
    female|a||Which row would catch it? Suppose clerks quietly let people who phoned in on the first day jump the queue. Which row flags it?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1cgle28'
    'female|a||The sign-up form: signing up on the first day is one of its nine answers, and winners would have far more of it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||One row in Oregon is out of balance on purpose.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The state drew people, but a winner's whole household could apply, so anyone who listed another household member held two tickets.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:150cb0h'
    female|a||Winners came from two-person households twice as often, so every Oregon estimate compares people within the same household size.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4i4zf8'
    'female|a||The check passes. But it checked only what can be seen: the hidden columns are trusted to the lottery, never proved by the table.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11grfd0'
    female|a||Why one joint test, rather than reading the rows of a balance table one at a time?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Because a fair draw still knocks the odd row out of line. Tested on its own at the usual five percent level, a row earns a star one time in twenty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:41gdxh'
    'female|a||Across: how many rows are tested. Up: the chance that at least one gets a star, if the rows were unrelated.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lt8ut0'
    female|a||Watch the point slide to more rows, and the chance of a false star climb.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uvjqyx'
    female|a||With Oregon's nine sign-up answers, it is already over a third.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||With twenty rows, almost two in three. A perfectly fair lottery usually shows a star somewhere.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4lcz8j'
    female|a||Real rows are related, since age and hospital stays move together, so the true chance is lower, here drawn for illustration. But a star or two is still what fairness looks like.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1l06yi2'
    'female|a||So a lone star is no alarm. A pattern is: many rows leaning the same way, and that is what the joint test weighs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jmrt8t'
    female|a||A new table. A trial's balance table has thirty rows. Two are starred, one tilted each way, and the joint test gives p = 0.4. What do you conclude?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ej2xaq'
    'female|a||Chance: thirty fair rows earn one or two stars on average, and a joint p of 0.4 finds no pattern.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||The alarm that does ring in real trials comes after the draw: who stays to be measured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Oregon''s winners were 1.6 points less likely to answer its mail survey, 49 percent against about 51: detectable, but small, and the people who did answer were still balanced.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:afj7l0'
    female|a||In the RAND insurance experiment of the 1970s, 87 percent of those on the most generous plan responded, against 63 percent on the least generous.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:62hbj8'
    female|a||A gap like that can undo a perfect draw, because the people who leave are not chosen by chance.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2lhyle'
    female|a||So, with a draw that passed its checks, what did coverage actually do in Oregon's first two years?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Winning raised the chance of being on Medicaid by about twenty-five points; some of those not drawn, about one in seven, got on anyway.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cj4q5e'
    female|a||So each gap between winners and losers is divided by that twenty-five-point jump. If winning mattered only through coverage, that gives the effect of coverage for the people the lottery put on Medicaid.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xld44m'
    female|a||In the first year, the covered were about a third more likely to have an outpatient visit, and a quarter less likely to have a medical bill sent to collectors.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1bkydan'
    female|a||About two years in, researchers interviewed and examined some twelve thousand people in and around Portland.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:apz3xt'
    'female|a||Doctor visits: five and a half a year among those not drawn, and about 2.7 more with coverage, somewhere between one and four and a half.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:rpm7vw'
    'female|a||Screening positive for depression: thirty percent among those not drawn, and about nine points fewer with coverage, a range from under two to almost seventeen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17x314h'
    'female|a||Out-of-pocket bills above thirty percent of income: five and a half percent, and nearly gone with coverage; this range, too, stays clear of zero.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jdx6yx'
    'female|a||A guess first. Blood pressure, cholesterol, blood sugar: what did two years of coverage do to them?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12g9mes'
    'female|a||No change the study could detect: each estimate sits near zero, with a range that runs past it both ways.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Blood pressure, blood sugar and cholesterol: no change the study could detect, and every range runs past zero both ways.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||But no detected change is not the same as no change. Blood pressure's range runs from about three points lower to two higher.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:o4hmsv'
    female|a||And here economists read the same rows differently.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15f98fc'
    female|a||Some take them as evidence that two years of coverage did little for these markers.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1tbg5p5'
    female|a||Others note that only about one person in twenty had high blood sugar at all, so the range is too wide to rule out a worthwhile effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1vnyc3i'
    female|a||What would tell them apart is many more people with diabetes in the study, or a longer wait.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ivvwwi'
    'female|a||Coverage did find more diabetes, though: new diagnoses up nearly four points, and diabetes medication up five.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1az9uqb'
    female|a||One new case. A city gives free bus passes by lottery to 2,000 of 6,000 applicants. The draw balances, and a year on, winners report more job interviews. What can you claim?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3jof6v'
    female|a||Among people who applied, the offer of a pass raised interviews. The draw settles that, and nothing wider.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So what does a coin buy? Not two identical groups, but a choice that cannot see the hidden columns, so they match on average on both sides.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||That cannot be tested directly. What can be checked is everything fixed before the draw, all together, and who stays to be measured.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:weiey5'
    'female|a||And the results are read by their ranges: in two years, Oregon''s coin moved care, money and mood, and left the body''s markers an open question.':
